    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0620" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.24/75: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-13T14:00:00-04:30">December 13, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. The Foreign Minister<anchor n="14" xml:id="d520-f1"/> has just requested me
                    to urge the most prompt action in supplying the following listed material to be
                    used for defense of the oil fields<anchor n="15" xml:id="d520-f2"/> already
                    requested through the Venezuelan Embassy Washington: 4 sets of anti-aircraft
                    machine guns caliber 0.50 including 16 pieces; 4 anti-aircraft batteries 37
                    millimeters including 16 pieces; 2,000 shells for each 37 millimeters cannon;
                    20,000 cartridges for each 0.50 machine gun. In order to expedite rapid delivery
                    of this material it was requested that it be sent from one of our bases in the
                    Caribbean. I urge prompt action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d520-f1" n="14" xml:id="d520-f1-content">
                <p>C. Parra Pérez.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d520-f2" n="15" xml:id="d520-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the concern of the United States over the defense of
                    the oil fields in Venezuela, see <ref target="#pg607">pp. 607</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
